<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Privacy policy</span>
  </nav>
</div>

<section class="wrap wrap-mid" style="padding-bottom:clamp(60px,8vw,110px)">
  <span class="eyebrow">Policy</span>
  <h1 style="margin:14px 0 18px">Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">What we collect, why we need it, how long we keep it and how to get it removed.</p>

  <div class="stack-32" style="margin-top:44px;font-size:0.94rem;line-height:1.9;color:var(--text-dim)">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Who is responsible for your data</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>The data controller for this shop is <strong class="gold"><%= company.legalName %></strong>, trading as
          <%= company.tradingName %>, of <%= company.addressLines.join(', ') %>. The person accountable for privacy
          questions is <%= company.contactPerson %>, reachable at
          <a class="link-underline" href="mailto:<%= company.privacyEmail %>"><%= company.privacyEmail %></a>.</p>
        <p>We handle personal data in accordance with Canada's <em>Personal Information Protection and Electronic
          Documents Act</em> (PIPEDA) and, where it applies to you, the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation.
          This policy is written to be read; it is the same undertaking either way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">What we collect, and why</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p><strong class="gold">To fulfil an order.</strong> Your name, email address, delivery address, and a contact
          telephone number where the carrier requires one. Without these we cannot ship, and under the terms of sale
          we cannot enter into the contract at all.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">To take payment.</strong> The card details you type at checkout are sent directly to
          <strong>OTT Pay</strong>, our payment processor. They are not sent to us. What is returned to us, and what
          our database keeps, is the card brand, the last four digits, the amount, the currency and the gateway's own
          payment and order identifiers — enough to reconcile an order, answer a query and issue a refund, and nothing
          more.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">To screen for fraud.</strong> Every card payment is scored for fraud risk before it is
          authorised. Where that service is enabled, a device-fingerprint script supplied by Kount runs in the
          checkout page and reports technical characteristics of your browser and device — screen size, time zone,
          installed fonts, whether the browser looks automated — to Kount. It does not read your files, your other
          tabs, or anything you have typed. If the service is not enabled, the checkout generates a session identifier
          locally instead and no data leaves our server for this purpose.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">To keep the shop working.</strong> Ordinary server logs record the IP address, the page
          requested and the time. We use them to keep the site up and to block abuse, and we keep them for 30
          days.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">What we never collect.</strong> We never ask for your full card number, its expiry date
          or its security code in any message, form or email outside the checkout — and anything that does is not from
          us. We never receive your bank login, and we do not run advertising or third-party analytics trackers on
          this site.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Cookies and local storage</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>We use the smallest set that will work. There is no consent banner because none of them is used for
          advertising or tracking:</p>
        <ul class="stack-8" style="padding-left:18px;list-style:disc">
          <li><span class="mono">cy_csrf</span> — a security token that stops another site from submitting our forms
            on your behalf. Strictly necessary, contains no personal data, expires after 30 days.</li>
          <li><span class="mono">cy_admin</span> — set only after a member of staff signs in to the back office. It is
            never set for a customer.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your basket lives in your browser's <span class="mono">localStorage</span> under the key
          <span class="mono">cy_cart_v1</span>, so that it survives a reload. It holds product identifiers and
          quantities and nothing else. Clearing your browser data empties it permanently.</p>
        <p>When a payment is submitted, the fraud-screening script described above runs in the checkout page. That is
          the only third-party code that executes during a visit, and it is loaded only on the checkout.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">How long we keep it</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>Order records, including the invoice and the card brand and last four digits, are kept for
          <strong class="gold">seven years</strong> after the end of the tax year in which you ordered. Tax law
          requires it and we cannot delete them early on request; everything else on the order we can.</p>
        <p>Server logs are kept for 30 days. Newsletter subscriptions are kept until you unsubscribe, which is one
          click in every email. A refund does not delete the order it relates to.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Who else receives it</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>Four parties, and no others:</p>
        <ul class="stack-8" style="padding-left:18px;list-style:disc">
          <li><strong>OTT Pay</strong> — the payment processor. Receives the card data you enter, your name, email
            address and billing address, plus the fraud-screening session identifier.</li>
          <li><strong>Kount</strong> — fraud screening, where enabled. Receives device characteristics and the order
            amount, not your name or address.</li>
          <li><strong>Our shipping carrier</strong> — receives your name, delivery address and a telephone number
            where one is required for delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Our hosting provider</strong> — stores the database and the logs on our behalf, under a data
            processing agreement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell, rent or trade personal data, and we do not pass it to anyone for their own marketing. We
          disclose it to anyone else only where the law compels us to, and where we are permitted to say so we will
          tell you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Where it is stored</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>Our database and backups are hosted in Canada. OTT Pay is a Canadian payment institution and processes the
          transaction in Canada. Kount is operated in the United States, so if you are in the European Economic Area
          the device data described above is transferred there under standard contractual clauses. Nothing else leaves
          Canada.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Your rights</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>You may ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, ask us to correct anything wrong, ask us
          to delete anything we are not obliged to keep, ask us to restrict what we do with it, object to processing,
          and ask for it in a portable machine-readable form. You may also withdraw consent at any time where consent
          is the basis for processing — for example by unsubscribing.</p>
        <p>Write to <a class="link-underline" href="mailto:<%= company.privacyEmail %>"><%= company.privacyEmail %></a>
          and we will respond within 30 days. There is no charge. We may ask you to confirm your identity first, so
          that we do not hand your data to somebody else.</p>
        <p>If you are not satisfied with our answer you may complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of
          Canada, or in the EU and UK to your national supervisory authority. We would rather you came to us first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Security, and children</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p>The site is served over TLS. Card data is transmitted directly from your browser to OTT Pay and never
          touches our servers, which is what keeps our own obligations under the card scheme rules at the lowest
          level. Passwords for the back office are stored as scrypt hashes, and the back office is reachable only over
          an authenticated session.</p>
        <p>This shop sells to adults. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 16, and if you
          believe a child has given us data, write to us and we will delete it.</p>
        <p>We may update this policy. The version that applies to your order is the one published when you placed it,
          and the date below changes whenever the text does.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">Contact</h3>
      <div class="stack-12">
        <p><%= company.legalName %><br />
          <% company.addressLines.forEach((line, i) => { %><%= line %><% if (i < company.addressLines.length - 1) { %><br /><% } %><% }) %></p>
        <p>Privacy: <a class="link-underline" href="mailto:<%= company.privacyEmail %>"><%= company.privacyEmail %></a><br />
          Everything else: <a class="link-underline" href="mailto:<%= company.email %>"><%= company.email %></a><br />
          Telephone: <a class="link-underline" href="tel:<%= company.phone.replace(/[^+0-9]/g, '') %>"><%= company.phone %></a></p>
        <p class="tiny faint">Last updated <%= policy.updated %>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row" style="gap:12px;margin-top:40px;flex-wrap:wrap">
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/terms">Terms of service</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/refund">Refund policy</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/shipping">Shipping policy</a>
    <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/contact">Contact us</a>
  </div>
</section>
